<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Qutb ud-Din Aibak</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Qutb ud-Din Aibak was a Turkic slave-general of the Ghurid ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-of-ghor">Muhammad of Ghor</a>, who governed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a> as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-india">viceroy</a> from 1192. After his master's death he declared himself independent ruler, founding the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluk</a> or <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk-dynasty-delhi">Slave Dynasty</a>. He is regarded as the founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi-sultanate">Delhi Sultanate</a> and began the construction of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qutb-minar">Qutb Minar</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/qutb-ud-din-aibak.jpg" alt="Qutb ud-Din Aibak" width="320" height="233" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Muhammad Umair Mirza · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grave_of_Sultan_Qutb_al-Din_Aibak.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
